  "question": {
    "text": "One of the by-products formed during the recovery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> from Solvay process is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaHCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The Solvay&nbsp;process is also called&nbsp;ammonia recovery.</p><p>The calcium hydroxide is reacted with the ammonium chloride separated out of the carbonating tower by filtration.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow/></mover><msub><msub><mi>CaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub></math></p><p>The ammonia is recycled back into the process to form ammoniated brine.</p><p>Calcium chloride is formed as a by-product of the Solvay process.</p>"
  }
